dings such as missing security headers or SPF/DMARC configuration","asset_type":"other","in_scope":false,"kind":"other","eligible_for_submission":null,"eligible_for_bounty":null}],"reward_types":["unknown"],"scope_kinds":["domain"],"summary_vi":null,"summary":"Flatpay takes vulnerability reports by email, covering any Flatpay domain or subdomain that publishes a security.txt file. Good-faith research under the policy counts as authorised and Flatpay won't pursue legal action over it. Reports can be anonymous and are acknowledged within 3 business days, with a PGP key supplied if more detail is needed. There's no paid bug bounty, but reporters of qualifying vulnerabilities are offered a Flatpay reward.","policy_url":"https://flatpay.com/responsible-disclosure","contact":"mailto:security@flatpay.com"},"self-host:freebsd-org":{"id":"self-host:freebsd-org","platform":"self-host","handle":"freebsd-org","name":"FreeBSD","url":"https://www.freebsd.org/security/reporting/","offers_bounty":false,"status":"open","stale":false,"last_seen":"2026-10-23T10:53:03Z","easy_score":0,"reasons":["chưa có dữ liệu scope"],"concrete_count":0,"min_bounty":null,"max_bounty":null,"currency":null,"first_seen":"2026-09-27T15:29:16Z","in_scope":[],"out_of_scope":[],"reward_types":["hall_of_fame"],"scope_kinds":[],"summary_vi":null,"summary":"Security issues in the FreeBSD operating system go to the Security Team by email, or PGP-encrypted to the Security Officer Team where a higher level of confidentiality is needed. Issues in the Ports Collection go to the Ports Security Team instead. A report should cover the vulnerability, affected versions, any workaround, a proof of concept and how the reporter wants crediting. The Security Officer favours full disclosure after a delay long enough to analyse, correct and test the problem.","policy_url":"https://www.freebsd.org/security/reporting/","contact":"mailto:secteam@FreeBSD.org"},"self-host:hckrt-com":{"id":"self-host:hckrt-com","platform":"self-hos